<report>
<title>Spearman's rank correlation</title>

<p>@sample_1 vs. @sample_2<br />
Observations per sample = @obs<br />
Spearman's score = @{ix:roundu}</p>

<p>Spearman's rank correlation coefficient (Rho) = @{rho:roundu}</p>

<block name="noci"><p><warn>CI not calculated when rho is 1 or -1.</warn></p></block>
<block name="ci"><p><ci>@{pc:round2}% CI for rho (Fisher's Z transformed) = @{from:roundu} to @{to:roundu}</ci></p></block>
<block name="lown">

<p><warn>Cannot consider probability with very small samples (n &lt; 4)</warn></p></block>
<block name="results">
<block name="nop"><p><warn>P not calculable</warn></p></block>
<block name="results">

<p><pval>Upper side @{p_u:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: positive correlation)<br />
<pval>Lower side @{p_l:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: negative correlation)<br />
<pval>Two sided @{p_2:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: any correlation)</p>
</block>
</block>
<block name="ties">

<p><pval>Ties present: exact P not used</pval></p>
</block>
</report>
